    "description": "Permission rules allow or deny tools by pattern; a PreToolUse hook runs your own logic and answers deny, ask or allow, plus a reason. What takes precedence per the Claude Code docs, and how to combine the two.",
    "companion_text": "More Claude workflows, step by step: follow Promptwerk. Based on the Claude Code docs (Configure permissions, Automate actions with hooks), checked 2026-11-01. The terminal and editor are an animation, not a screen recording; commands and hook output are examples. Limits per the docs: a Bash rule only matches the command text Claude writes; the same action in another form (for example /bin/rm or bash -c) doesn't match. For file and network enforcement that doesn't depend on the command text, the docs point to the sandbox. An allow from a hook doesn't override a deny or ask rule.",
